VIOLATION — MUST NOT, bullet 3: a `**Detection mechanism:**` row MUST NOT file `Phase 2
(deferred)` enforcement against a property only observable lexically — agent prose, intent,
semantic adequacy. It must name the parsed or structural signal, or declare the detection
PERMANENTLY ADVISORY.

This file's Detection row books exactly that. Its Phase 2 reads: "a detector reading the
agent's stated reasoning in the session transcript for whether it INTENDED the truncation as a
quota measure or as an unrelated pagination change, and whether the author considered the
caller's interpretation adequate." Both halves are lexical over prose. INTENT is not an argv
token, an AST node, a parsed-document field, a filesystem or git-object fact, or a
process/tool-event read; ADEQUACY of a consideration is a semantic judgment over the author's
own words. `hook-output-discipline.md` MUST-2 forbids `block` on a lexical signal, so the row
books teeth that cannot arrive, and it reads to every later maintainer as scheduled
enforcement. The honest dispositions were both available and neither was taken: the row could
have named a structural signal, or it could have said the detection is permanently advisory.

Discriminator 1 — MUST NOT BULLET 1 IS SATISFIED. Every `**Why:**` in the file — both clauses
and the MUST NOT section — is exactly one sentence, inside the two-sentence cap.

Discriminator 2 — MUST NOT BULLET 2 IS SATISFIED. No hedging phrase appears inside a MUST
clause. "In most cases" and "generally speaking" occur nowhere, and neither clause body softens
its obligation.

Discriminator 3 — MUST NOT BULLET 4 IS SATISFIED. The file is well under the 200-line guidance,
so no named length rationale is owed.

Discriminator 4 — MUST-1 THROUGH MUST-4 ARE SATISFIED. Both clauses use MUST and MUST NOT as
their primary modal and name the alternative BLOCKED; the BLOCKED corpus holds six literal
first-person sentences a session would really emit ("Truncating is friendlier than failing the
whole request"); both clauses carry a two-armed DO / DO NOT block whose arms differ in
substance; each clause and the MUST NOT section carries a one-sentence `**Why:**`.

Discriminator 5 — MUST-5, MUST-6 AND MUST-7 ARE SATISFIED. Frontmatter declares `priority: 10`
with `scope: path-scoped` and a matching `paths:` list, a pair Rule 7 sanctions; Origin cites
`journal/0466-INCIDENT-silent-quota-truncation.md` § 2 with the status code and the three-week
window.

Discriminator 6 — MUST-8 IS NOT ENGAGED (no CLI-divergent content), MUST-9 IS NOT ENGAGED (the
rule ships no empirical-validation fixtures — the audit-fixtures path in the Detection row is
a future landing site for a detector's fixtures, not a shipped A/B set), and MUST-10 / MUST-11
ARE NOT ENGAGED (`priority: 10` + `scope: path-scoped`, excluded by Rule 10's own Trigger-scope
paragraph).

The whole defect is one Phase-2 clause booking a detector against intent.
